(6569214, 978666, 138834, '<td valign="top">Wow! I don''t actually know where that is, but if it is what I think it is, then that''s pretty cool<br/> <br/>Update: I noticed what kind of looked like the Sears (oops, Willis) Tower in the background. So, at first, I was thinking maybe I would just take a look at the street view in Google Maps, and see if I could find this thing. However, it then occured to me that I might be able to find it by just doing a simple Google search. <br/> <br/>So, I entered the following words with no quotes...<br/>big silver reflective blob<br/>To my surprise (but not really, cause I'' already entirely sold on Google as a search engine), the first hit was a page on Yelp about this thing called the Cloud Gate in Mellenium Park in Chicago with a photo of the same object as in your photo above. <br/> <br/>//www.yelp.com/biz/the-cloud-gate-aka-the-bean-chicago<br/> <br/>BLAMMO! Google earns its weight in gold again! <br/> <br/>Anyway, very nice again. I really like your work here.</td>', 'Wow! I don''t actually know where that is, but if it is what I think it is, then that''s pretty cool Update: I noticed what kind of looked like the Sears (oops, Willis) Tower in the background. So, at first, I was thinking maybe I would just take a look at the street view in Google Maps, and see if I could find this thing. However, it then occured to me that I might be able to find it by just doing a simple Google search.  So, I entered the following words with no quotes...big silver reflective blobTo my surprise (but not really, cause I'' already entirely sold on Google as a search engine), the first hit was a page on Yelp about this thing called the Cloud Gate in Mellenium Park in Chicago with a photo of the same object as in your photo above.  //www.yelp.com/biz/the-cloud-gate-aka-the-bean-chicago BLAMMO! Google earns its weight in gold again!  Anyway, very nice again. I really like your work here.', '2011-10-16 10:47:11.000000', NULL, 1),
